    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "passed 867 billion dollar farm bill. And you serve on the Agriculture Committee. And of course, you also the founder and co-chair of the ABCU congressional bipartisan caucus. And so we're just honored to have you join the broadcast today and give us your take and provide some perspective and analysis on the passage of this bill. So let's talk about that now. I do note that the The wonderful thing about this is that Congress has been asked to take on the elimination of a provision of a law that for decades required 1890 land grant universities to spend most of their federal extension money in a calendar year. And so with that in mind and all the other things happening with the bill, what does that mean, Congressman, for the 19 land grant HBCUs?",
