    "turn_text": "put, I had a bill in the State House and we tried to fix it and then they sort of dwindled back to where they were. So what this will do is basically provide some, now as you said transparency, But we will be able to, as a Congress, to see what these states are doing. Now, and I just think that sometimes you have to shed the light on one thing so that our colleagues will really see that we're not just talking about this, but we're able to show that some of the states are not being treated fairly. And that has a negative impact on our schools when they don't get it. And give you a good example of North Carolina, North Carolina State, I understand, get the 600% match, 600%. North Carolina. What does it all",
