    "turn_text": "If you're just joining us, you tune in to the HBCU Nation radio show. I'm your host Anthony Ray. Glad to have you join the broadcast today. The $867 billion from Bill recently passed by Congress includes major wins for land grant institutions, especially HBCUs. And we're blessed to have joining us for this segment, our good friend, Congresswoman Alma Adams, Democrat North Carolina 12th District. Councilman Adams is a member of the Committee on Agriculture and was to come free with the whole bill and everything that was related to getting it passed. She's also the founder and co-chair of the HBCU Congressional bipartisan caucus and she's joined us today to give us her take and provide some perspective and analysis on the passage of the bill. Again, my good friend, Councilman Adams, welcome to the show.",
