    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96498.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 116,
    "turn_text": "Okay, well, listen, we've got a lot of things that we want to do. We will continue to elevate this national dialogue, which was one of our goals from the outset when we established the bipartisan caucus, so we're going to keep educating members of Congress and staff on the impact that our schools have. And we're going to continue to try to pull together where we can by partisan legislation that will address some of the issues that our schools have. In the Farm Bill, the USDA will be involved in terms of the rulemaking. And so we're going to be fully involved in that because they're going to be administering, you know, all these things that are in this bill and we want to make sure that they do what is required. So we will be conducting oversight of USDA to make sure that the rules are effective and that they are helping who these regulations were intended to help. Also, you know, we haven't heard a whole lot from the White House initiative on HBCUs, but we want to continue to hold everybody who's connected in any way accountable, making sure that they carry out their mission. We will look for increased grant opportunities for our schools, across all of the federal agencies, and making sure that the schools have that information and that And that things are equal and fair. You know, some of the things that I talked about earlier in terms of corrections that we had to make in the law was because things are just not, you know, we don't have a level playing skills. So we want to, we're going to stay on top of that. And then of course, the Higher Education Act will be reauthorized and certainly I'm sure Bobby Scott, who will be heading up the education",
